                 ·)^» ToyAdder v1.O for DayDream BBS «^(·

         Programmed by Joo/ToyTools with ASM-One v1.28b by T.F.A.


  Introduction:

  ToyAdder is a textadder which adds two adverts, one to the front of a text
  file and one to the end. ToyAdder is designed to use with DayDream BBS, and
  it needs DayDream's uploadlog and userbase to work properly. You can use
  special codes in both of the adverts to add the filename, uploader etc.
  You can have a list of adverts where from ToyAdder randomly chooses the
  header and tailer. ToyAdder doesn't advertise itself in the text and the
  only visible thing is the little banner text during the filecheck.


  How to install ToyAdder:

  -  Put "ToyAdder" to "DayDream:Utils/" and "ToyAdder.doc" to
     "DayDream:Docs/".

  -  Put "ToyAdder.headers" and "ToyAdder.tailers" files to DayDream's
     config directory. (usually "DayDream:Configs/")
     ToyAdder gets this directory from "ENV:DreamUtils".

     Edit these files so that the number of adverts and the paths are
     right. Put "0" to the number of adverts if you don't want that kind
     of advert. ToyAdder picks a random advert from the list or if there
     is only one advert then that will be used.

3                                  <= this is the number of adverts.
DayDream:Adverts/TextAdvert.1      <= advert's full path and filename.
DayDream:Adverts/TextAdvert.2      <= ...
DayDream:Adverts/TextAdvert.3      <= ... 
                                      ... until all adverts are listed.

     Remember to add a linefeed after each line!

  -  Add ToyAdder to DayDream's filetypes. Use it as a filechecker in the
     ARC_TEST field. Add ToyAdder to all the textfiletypes (TXT,NFO,DOC etc.)
     you want. ToyAdder can be used as a offline checker, too.

ARC_TYPE...... F
ARC_EXTENSION. TXT
ARC_NAME...... Text file
ARC_TEST...... DayDream:Utils/ToyAdder %A	<= add this.
ARC_FAIL1..... -
ARC_FAIL2..... -
ARC_FAIL3..... -
ARC_FIDEXTRACT System:Commands/TxtExtract e FILE_ID.DIZ %A
ARC_FIDADD.... System:Commands/TxtExtract a FILE_ID.DIZ %A
ARC_VIEW...... C:Type %A
ARC_OFFLINE... N				<= can be used, too.
ARC_GETDATE... N
ARC_DELETECOR. N
ARC_DISPLAY... Y
ARC_SECVIEW... 180

  You can use following codes in the adverts to add certain info. The number
  in the parantheses is the field width. So you need that many characters for
  the text (eg. %h34567890123456789012345 or %f3456789012345678). If there is
  no value (-) then there is no field width and no space is needed.

  %h = handle (25)            Uploader's handle (25 characters)
  %H = handle (-)             Uploader's handle
  %r = handle (10)            Uploader's handle (10 characters)
  %R = handle (15)            Uploader's handle (15 characters)
  %o = organization (25)      Uploader's organization (25 characters)
  %O = organization (-)	      Uploader's organization
  %g = organization (15)      Uploader's organization (15 characters)
  %b = bps rate (5)           Uploader's bps rate (5 characters)
  %B = bps rate (-)           Uploader's bps rate
  %n = node (2)               Uploader's node (2 characters)
  %N = node (-)               Uploader's node
  %f = file name (18)         File name (18 characters)
  %F = file name (-)          File name
  %a = file name (12)         File name (12 characters, /X style)
  %s = file size (8)          File size (8 characters)
  %S = file size (-)          File size
  %d = upload date (9)        Upload date (9 characters) (eg. 24-Dec-95)
  %D = upload date (8)        Upload date (8 characters) (eg. 24.12.95)
  %t = upload time (8)        Upload time (8 characters) (eg. 10:21:12)
  %w = week day (9)           Upload weekday (9 characters) (eg. Monday)
  %W = week day (-)           Upload weekday
  %u = upload signature (44)  Uploader's trademark (44 characters)


